course: dictionary
lesson: 3828
title: Former: earlier, or the first of two
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Former means earlier, from a time before now. «The former head teacher» used to lead the school, but she does not any more. The clue is the time: something that is former has already happened.
explain: Use the word before a noun, as in «a former champion» or «former pupil». Check by swapping in «earlier» or «from before»: «an earlier champion» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Two words work as a pair: «the former» is the first of two things just mentioned, and «the latter» is the second. «Cats and dogs are common pets: the former purr, the latter bark.» Cats purr, so the former means cats. Dogs bark, so the latter means dogs.
explain: In design technology, a former is a frame or shape that something is formed around, like the solid shape a balloon is dipped onto. This is a different meaning, so check the subject you are reading about.
fact: Former means earlier, from before but not now.
fact: «The former head teacher» means someone who used to be head teacher.
fact: «The former» means the first of two things just mentioned, and «the latter» means the second.
fact: «The Aral Sea has shrunk to about a tenth of its former size», so its earlier size was much bigger.
fact: In design technology, a former is a shape that something is formed or coated around.
exercise: «The former champion came back to watch the final.» What does former mean here? | A referee who blows the whistle | Someone who is very tall | *Someone who won before, but is not champion now | Someone who will win the next match
exercise: «Cats and dogs are common pets: the former purr, the latter bark.» What does the former mean? | Owners | Dogs | Pets | *Cats
exercise: «The Aral Sea has shrunk to about a tenth of its former size.» What does its former size mean? | Its size in the future | Its shape on a map | Its size after it grew | *Its size from before, when it was bigger
test: Ruth says, «My former school was near the park.» What does former tell you? | Ruth goes there every day | She has never been to a school | *She used to go to that school, but not now | She is going there next year
test: «John Newton was a former slave-ship captain who changed his life.» What does former tell you about him? | He is still a captain today | *He had been a captain before, but later changed his life | He was a sailor, not a captain | He will be a captain soon
exam: Tom and Sam both trained hard. «The former won the race, and the latter came second.» Who came second? | Neither of them | Both of them | *Sam | Tom
